2.How much semantic meaning does a <div> tag provide to search engines?
A)High importance
B)Medium importance
C)No semantic meaning  //answers
D)Only for images

Correct Answer: ✅ C. No semantic meaning

Explanation (Simple)

The <div> tag is a generic container used to group HTML elements for styling or layout.

It does not describe the content inside it.
Search engines do not get any semantic meaning from a <div>.
For meaningful structure, use semantic HTML tags like <header>, <nav>, <main>, <section>, <article>, and <footer>.

Example:

<div>
  <h1>Welcome</h1>
  <p>This is a website.</p>
</div>

Here, <div> only groups the content—it doesn't tell search engines what the content represents.

✅ Correct Answer: C. No semantic meaning



3.What is the impact of using too many nested <div> tags (often called "Divitis")?
A)The browser crashes
B)Makes the code hard to read and maintain  //anwers
C)Improves SEO
D)Increases download speed

✅ Correct Answer: B. Makes the code hard to read and maintain

Explanation (Simple)

Using too many nested <div> tags (called "Divitis") creates unnecessary layers in your HTML.

Problems:

❌ Makes the code difficult to read.
❌ Harder to maintain and debug.
❌ Makes the HTML structure more complex than necessary.

Bad Example:

<div>
  <div>
    <div>
      <p>Hello</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

Better Example:

<section>
  <p>Hello</p>
</section>

Using semantic tags like <section>, <article>, or <main> makes your HTML cleaner and easier to understand.

✅ Correct Answer: B. Makes the code hard to read and maintain


4.In the box model, which part of the <div> is the space between the content and the border?
A)Margin
B)Padding  //answers
C)Outline
D)Gap


✅ Correct Answer: B. Padding

Explanation (Simple)

In the CSS Box Model:

Content → The actual text or image.
Padding → Space between the content and the border.
Border → The line around the padding and content.
Margin → Space outside the border.
Visual:
+---------------------------+
|         Margin            |
|  +---------------------+  |
|  |      Border         |  |
|  |  +---------------+  |  |
|  |  |   Padding     |  |  |
|  |  | +-----------+ |  |  |
|  |  | | Content   | |  |  |
|  |  | +-----------+ |  |  |
|  |  +---------------+  |  |
|  +---------------------+  |
+---------------------------+

✅ Correct Answer: B. Padding


